   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re in Cerulean City — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center and a Mart; tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. From here: NORTH → Route 24 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; SOUTH → Route 5 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; EAST → Route 9 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; WEST → Route 4 — wild Pokémon to catch/train, a Pokémon Center. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 3; Route 25; Route 10. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. You have SURF — you can cross water.. Okay — to get past this I need Mewtwo — the strongest Pokemon in the game, at the bottom of Cerulean Cave. The guard only steps aside for the Champion, and the Master Ball has been waiting for exactly this moment.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. YOU WON — you\'re the CHAMPION and the credits have rolled. This is the post-game victory lap: head OUT of the league building, heal the team up, and pick your own adventures now (Cerulean Cave just opened to champions, and the Pokédex is far from full). Nothing is required anymore — this is your world to enjoy. YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): All eight Gym Badges are yours. The Elite Four and the Champion are the summit.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "OAK. Er-hem! Congratulations, KIRA! This floor is the POK.MON HALL OF FAME. POK.MON LEAGUE CHAMPIONS are honored for their exploits here. Their POK.MON are also"; "OAK. Er-hem! Congratulations, KIRA! This floor is the POK.MON HALL OF FAME. POK.MON LEAGUE CHAMPIONS are honored for their exploits here. Their POK.MON are also"; "I had a vision of your arrival. I have had psychic powers since I was a child. It started when a spoon I carelessly tossed, bent. I dislike battling, but if you"; "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective. Next: FIRST Mewtwo — the strongest Pokemon in the game, at the bottom of Cerulean Cave. The guard only steps aside for the Champion, and the Master Ball has been waiting for exactly this moment — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road. Bigger picture: Enjoy the post-game as Champion (Cerulean Cave, the Pokédex). Your team right now: blastoise (L94), moltres (L56), articuno (L53), zapdos (L55). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "8 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow, Soul, Marsh, Volcano, Earth). You're the CHAMPION — the game is beaten. This is the post-game victory lap. Pokédex: 20 caught. Champion. The credits rolled — everything from here is the victory lap (Cerulean Cave, the Pokédex, her world 